// Tags: attack.defense-impairment, attack.t1685
// Description: Detects execution of EDR-Freeze, a tool that exploits the MiniDumpWriteDump function and WerFaultSecure.exe to suspend EDR and Antivirus processes on Windows.
// EDR-Freeze leverages a race-condition attack to put security processes into a dormant state by suspending WerFaultSecure at the moment it freezes the target process.
// This technique does not require kernel-level exploits or BYOVD, but instead abuses user-mode functionality to temporarily disable monitoring by EDR or Antimalware solutions.
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

(((src.process.image.path containsCIS "\\EDR-Freeze" OR src.process.image.path containsCIS "\\EDRFreeze") AND src.process.image.path endswithCIS ".exe") OR ((Hashes containsCIS "IMPHASH=1195F7935954A2CD09157390C33F8E8C" OR Hashes containsCIS "IMPHASH=129F58DE3D687FB7F012BF6C3D679997" OR Hashes containsCIS "IMPHASH=2C617A175D0086251642C6619F7CC8BA" OR Hashes containsCIS "IMPHASH=8828F0B906F7844358FB92A899E9520F" OR Hashes containsCIS "IMPHASH=AF76D95157EC554DC1EF178E4E66D447" OR Hashes containsCIS "IMPHASH=E1B04316B61ACA31DD52ABBEC0A37FD5" OR Hashes containsCIS "IMPHASH=8B2D5B54AFCFEC60D54F6B31D80ED4A0" OR Hashes containsCIS "IMPHASH=AB8BB31EDD91D2A05FE7B62A535E9EB7")))
